REM node.pni: one sourced batch for one node, after the Sanskrit parser's own workflow.
REM © 1993–2026 Abhishek Choudhary. All rights reserved. AyeAI.

CYCLER NODE
  TITLE   "One batch, sourced to tested"
  SCRIPT  "تجزیہ"
  OUTPUT  RESEARCH
  UNIT    "batch"
  PURPOSE "Bring one coherent batch of rules for one node from a citable source into tested code."

  CONTRACT
    REFUSE    "a rule without a source"
    REFUSE    "a disagreement between sources resolved without a record"
    INVARIANT "the Python and JavaScript ports stay behaviour-identical"
    EVIDENCE  "the source URL, retrieval date and SHA-256 of what was retrieved"
  END CONTRACT

  STAGE CONCEPT
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT JSON
    INTO   batch
    ASK
      I am adding one batch of rules to one tajziya node. Reply with only this JSON:
      {"node":"registry id","stage":"...","script":"ISO 15924 code","batch":"one section or one rule type","engine":"an id from registry/engines.json"}
      What I have so far:
      {seed}
    END ASK
    VALIDATE HAS(batch, "engine")
    ON FAIL CLARIFY
  END STAGE

  STAGE SOURCE
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   VERIFY
    EXPECT JSON
    FROM   batch
    INTO   batch.source
    ASK
      Take the batch from a real, citable edition. Record the URL, the retrieval date, an
      archived copy, the SHA-256 of what was retrieved, and the licence or terms.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE CROSSCHECK
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   VERIFY
    EXPECT JSON
    FROM   batch
    INTO   batch.disagreements
    ASK
      Where more than one source covers these rules, list every disagreement in numbering,
      wording or classification. Record both readings and state which one the node follows,
      with the reason.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE IMPLEMENT
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   batch
    INTO   batch.change
    ASK
      Add the data in the existing schema and implement the batch in the node's port. If the
      node has a JavaScript twin, port the change there in the same batch.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE TEST
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   EXECUTE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   batch
    INTO   batch.tests
    ASK
      Test against attested examples from the source, not only against the code's own output.
      Run python3 tests/parity.py where there is a JavaScript twin, then bash ops/verify.sh,
      and paste the outputs verbatim.
    END ASK
    GATE   HUMAN "BATCH accepted"
  END STAGE
END CYCLER
